// The tier of every chemistry reagent that has a block structure (doc/rewrite/proposals/chemistry_redesign.md section 8; the book shows it).
//
//   1  staples        one or two steps; the dispenser and the stocked precursors; gentle or warm heat; no solid catalyst. Each has a dirty shortcut (a process chemical
//                     poured in, or a one-pot recipe that leaves trace-potent contaminants).
//   2  standard       two or three steps: a staple and one more process.
//   3  advanced       three or more steps; an enzyme or a catalytic metal sheet (another department's feedstock) on the way, or a strong oxidiser.
//   4  exotic         an exotic core that cannot be made on the station (not converted yet).
// The building blocks, the intermediates and the metals are tier 1: they are what the rest is made of.

/// reagent id => tier (CHEM_TIER_*).
